<title>FRANCE: U.S. principal Q1 originator of Paris air cargo.</title>
<headline>U.S. principal Q1 originator of Paris air cargo.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in January-March 1997, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The principal countries of origin for ADP imports during the first three months of this year, with percentage change on January-March 1996 in parentheses, were as follows:</p>
<p>1. United States    36,778 tonnes   (-0.5 percent)</p>
<p>2. Japan		 6,448 tonnes  (+51.0)</p>
<p>3. India		 6,094 tonnes  (-13.7)</p>
<p>4. Canada		5,709 tonnes  (-19.5)</p>
<p>5. UK		    5,394 tonnes  (+36.4)</p>
<p>6. Hong Kong	   4,691 tonnes  (+10.4)</p>
<p>7. Germany	     3,962 tonnes  (+22.8)</p>
<p>8. Thailand	    3,633 tonnes  (+47.4)</p>
<p>9. Senegal	     3,044 tonnes  (+16.8)</p>
<p>10. Italy		2,641 tonnes   (-8.7)</p>
<p>11. Fr.W Indies	2,587 tonnes   (+7.8)</p>
<p>12. Singapore	  2,443 tonnes  (+72.9)</p>
<p>13. Kenya		2,275 tonnes  (-23.9)</p>
<p>14. Morocco	    1,981 tonnes  (-30.9)</p>
<p>15. Argentina	  1,809 tonnes   (+5.6)</p>
<p>16. Korea		1,780 tonnes  (+46.3)</p>
<p>17. Egypt		1,610 tonnes  (+28.2)</p>
<p>18. China		1,594 tonnes  (+56.4)</p>
<p>19. Switzerland	1,540 tonnes  (+23.9)</p>
<p>20. U.A.E.	     1,401 tonnes  (-24.5)</p>
<p>January-March 1997 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 134,296 tonnes, an increase of 4.2 percent on the same period last year, ADP, figures show.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel +44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
</text>
